body:
Layered template library: a deck's template library is one merged set drawn from up to two library layers (library-layer). The external layer is the library directory named by the top-level `templates:` key in `kalide.yaml` when the key is present (external-template-library); the local layer is the deck-root `templates/` directory. The external layer is loaded when the key is present, the local layer is loaded whenever the deck-root `templates/` directory exists, and both are loaded when both are present; with no key the local layer alone is the library. The two layers have equal standing and merge into one library — one set of slides, sections, themes and media — with no precedence between them, so a deck resolves a slide or section template by name and a theme by name against the merged set (library-layer-uniqueness). A reference written inside a template or theme resolves within that template's or theme's own layer — its `media` helper, `media:` and `theme:<name>/` references and files — except a local template's `section` helper call, which resolves against the merged section namespace (library-layer-references). Each layer's files are read from that layer's own root, and an error raised while loading a layer names that root (error-reporting). A deck with no layer — no key and no deck-root `templates/` directory — fails per templates-dir-required.

AC:
- a deck with `templates: ../shared-lib` and a deck-root `templates/` loads both layers: a slide defined in `../shared-lib` and a slide defined in the local `templates/` both serve in one deck;
- a deck with `templates: ../shared-lib` and no local `templates/` loads the external layer alone;
- a deck with no `templates:` key and a local `templates/` loads the local layer alone;
- a deck with no key and no local `templates/` fails naming the expected local `templates/`;
- an error from the external layer names the external root, and an error from the local layer names the local root.
